title":["LSTM, ConvLSTM, MDN-RNN and GridLSTM Memory-based Deep Reinforcement Learning"],"author":[{"given":"Fernando","family":"Duarte","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institute of Electronics and Informatics Engineering of Aveiro, University of Aveiro, Aveiro, Portugal, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Nuno","family":"Lau","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronics, Telecommunications and Informatics, University of Aveiro, Aveiro, Portugal, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Artur","family":"Pereira","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronics, Telecommunications and Informatics, University of Aveiro, Aveiro, Portugal, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Lu\u00eds","family":"Reis","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Engineering, Department of Informatics Engineering, University of Porto, Porto, Portugal, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0011664900003393","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 15th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.51483\/ijaiml.6.5s.2026.379-392","title":["DRIFTBENCH: Long-Horizon Memory Benchmark For AI Agents"],"author":[{"given":"Sunil Kumar","family":"P","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Seethi Venkata","family":"Sai Gowtham Reddi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sai Chaitanya","family":"P","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.51483\/ijaiml.6.5s.2026.379-392","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["International Journal of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning"]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6349019","title":["Persistent Memory Architectures for Personal Artificial Intelligence Systems"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0008-6375-3217","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Arshdeep","family":"Bhardwaj","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.6349019","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Recent advances in large language models have significantly expanded the capabilities of conversational artificial intelligence systems. Transformer-based architectures enable models capable of reasoning, summarization, and natural language interaction across a wide range of domains. Despite these advances, most deployed systems remain fundamentally stateless. Interactions are typically constrained by bounded context windows and lack persistent understanding of individual users. This limitation restricts the development of truly personal artificial intelligence systems capable of long-term interaction, adaptation, and cognitive support. Human cognition develops across time through accumulated experiences and reflection. Artificial intelligence systems that cannot store and interpret long-term memory remain limited in their ability to support these processes. This paper proposes a conceptual framework for persistent memory in personal artificial intelligence systems. We introduce a layered memory architecture consisting of conversational memory, semantic memory, and reflective memory. These memory layers enable artificial intelligence systems to maintain evolving representations of individuals and support long-term interaction. Persistent memory architectures may therefore represent a foundational component of next-generation personal artificial intelligence systems designed to augment human reflection, decision-making, and cognitive processes.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.017","title":["Planning with Uncertainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.017","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025","title":["2025 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp;amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]}},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.014","title":["Learning with Uncertainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.014","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.021","title":["Individuals and Relations"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.021","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.024","title":["The Big Picture"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.024","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.008","title":["Propositions and Inference"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.008","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.026","title":["Retrospect and Prospect"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.026","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.030","title":["Index of Algorithms"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.030","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.013","title":["Reasoning with Uncertainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.013","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.007","title":["Reasoning with Constraints"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.007","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1145\/3811238","title":["Proceedings of the 2026 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Agents"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/3811238","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,27]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,5]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,27]]}},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.006","title":["Searching for Solutions"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.006","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1515\/9783111439273-019","title":["Memory and Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"given":"Anna","family":"Poletti","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1515\/9783111439273-019","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,18]]},"container-title":["Dynamics, Mediation, Mobilization"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.011","title":["Supervised Machine Learning"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.011","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1162\/isal_a_00605","title":["Towards a Theory of Mind for Artificial Intelligence Agents"],"author":[{"given":"Jory","family":"Schossau","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Arend","family":"Hintze","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1162\/isal_a_00605","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["The 2023 Conference on Artificial Life"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0013262100003890","title":["PurGE: Towards Responsible Artificial Intelligence Through Sustainable Hyperparameter Optimization"],"author":[{"given":"Gauri","family":"Vaidya","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Information Systems, University of Limerick, Ireland"},{"name":"Lero the Research Ireland Centre for Software, Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Meghana","family":"Kshirsagar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Information Systems, University of Limerick, Ireland"},{"name":"Lero the Research Ireland Centre for Software, Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Conor","family":"Ryan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Information Systems, University of Limerick, Ireland"},{"name":"Lero the Research Ireland Centre for Software, Ireland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0013262100003890","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 17th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1201\/9781003410980-4","title":["Memory in Cells"],"author":[{"given":"Huijue","family":"Jia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1201\/9781003410980-4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,30]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,30]]},"container-title":["Neuroscience for Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-032-29770-9_18","title":["Shaping Credibility Judgments in\u00a0Human\u2013GenAI Partnership via\u00a0Weaker LLMs: A Transactive Memory Perspective on\u00a0AI Literacy"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6075-2832","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Md Touhidul","family":"Islam","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6884-0119","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mahir","family":"Akgun","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5063-3808","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Syed","family":"Billah","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-032-29770-9_18","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2027]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,27]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,27]]},"container-title":["Lecture Notes in Computer Science","Artificial Intelligence in Education"]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.5332489","title":["When Machines Remember Pain: Affective Memory Encoding and Behavioral Adaptation in Artificial Agents"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-8812-0807","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Lefliti","family":"Mohamed","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.5332489","issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This paper presents a novel approach to artificial memory encoding by introducing affective memory units into a reinforcement learning agent. Unlike traditional agents that rely solely on reward signals, our agent encodes experiences as symbolic memory units: \u03b6 = (x, t, \u03c6, \u03b5, \u03bc, a) Where:-x denotes affective state (e.g., curiosity, frustration)-t is internal time-\u03c6 is the perceptual state-\u03b5 is the intensity of the experience-\u03bc is its structural impact (positive or negative)-a is the action taken We demonstrate that the agent can recall painful experiences (*\u03bc &amp;lt; 0*) and adapt its behavior to avoid repeating them. This marks a conceptual shift toward agents with proto-subjective memory, capable of affect-driven decision-making. The implications span AI safety, cognitive modeling, and the philosophy of machine selfhood.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.ailsci.2025.100141","title":["From task-specific language models to research agents"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0557-5714","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"J\u00fcrgen","family":"Bajorath","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.ailsci.2025.100141","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,12]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,12]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence in the Life Sciences"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai59313.2023.10452470","title":["Artificial Intelligence and its Effectiveness in Modern Teaching"],"author":[{"given":"Hanadi Mohammad","family":"Alomran","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Taibah University","place":["Madinah, Saudi Arabia"],"department":["Department of Computer Science"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Omar Hussain","family":"Alhazmi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Taibah University","place":["Madinah, Saudi Arabia"],"department":["Department of Computer Science"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai59313.2023.10452470","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,12]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,12]]},"container-title":["2023 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.artint.2024.104131","title":["Discrete preference games with logic-based agents: Formal framework, complexity, and islands of tractability"],"author":[{"given":"Gianluigi","family":"Greco","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3323-9328","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Marco","family":"Manna","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.artint.2024.104131","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,7]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,7]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-030-93789-8_67-1","title":["Transactive Memory System"],"author":[{"given":"Mar\u00eda del Pilar","family":"Garc\u00eda-Chitiva","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-030-93789-8_67-1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,3,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["The Palgrave Encyclopedia of Memory Studies"]},{"DOI":"10.3233\/faia250967","title":["MemoCue: Empowering LLM-Based Agents for Human Memory Recall via Strategy-Guided Querying"],"author":[{"given":"Qian","family":"Zhao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zhuo","family":"Sun","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Bin","family":"Guo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zhiwen","family":"Yu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3233\/faia250967","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Agent-assisted memory recall is one critical research problem in the field of human-computer interaction. In conventional methods, the agent can retrieve information from its equipped memory module to help the person recall incomplete or vague memories. The limited size of memory module hinders the acquisition of complete memories and impacts the memory recall performance in practice. Memory theories suggest that the person\u2019s relevant memory can be proactively activated through some effective cues. Inspired by this, we propose a novel strategy-guided agent-assisted memory recall method, allowing the agent to transform an original query into a cue-rich one via the judiciously designed strategy to help the person recall memories. To this end, there are two key challenges. (1) How to choose the appropriate recall strategy for diverse forgetting scenarios with distinct memory-recall characteristics? (2) How to obtain the high-quality responses leveraging recall strategies, given only abstract and sparsely annotated strategy patterns? To address the challenges, we propose a Recall Router framework. Specifically, we design a 5W Recall Map to classify memory queries into five typical scenarios and define fifteen recall strategy patterns across the corresponding scenarios. We then propose a hierarchical recall tree combined with the Monte Carlo Tree Search algorithm to optimize the selection of strategy and the generation of strategy responses. We construct an instruction tuning dataset and fine-tune multiple open-source large language models (LLMs) to develop MemoCue, an agent that excels in providing memory-inspired responses. Experiments on three representative datasets show that MemoCue surpasses LLM-based methods by 17.74% in recall inspiration. Further human evaluation highlights its advantages in memory-recall applications.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence and Applications","ECAI 2025"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0012307100003636","title":["Models with Verbally Enunciated Explanations: Towards Safe, Accountable, and Trustworthy Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"given":"Mattias","family":"Wahde","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Chalmers University of Technology, SE-412 96 Gothenburg, Sweden, --- Select a Country ---"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0012307100003636","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1515\/9783112223062-019","title":["427Index"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1515\/9783112223062-019","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,1]]},"container-title":["Agentic Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.4324\/9781003227458-16","title":["Transactive Memory Systems and Learning"],"author":[{"given":"Leila","family":"Bighash","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Michael","family":"Farzinpour","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4324\/9781003227458-16","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,3]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,3]]},"container-title":["Group Communication"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.027","title":["Mathematical Preliminaries and Notation"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.027","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.3233\/faia251160","title":["Mem0: Building Production-Ready AI Agents with Scalable Long-Term Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Prateek","family":"Chhikara","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Mem0.ai, research@mem0.ai"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dev","family":"Khant","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Mem0.ai, research@mem0.ai"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Saket","family":"Aryan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Mem0.ai, research@mem0.ai"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Taranjeet","family":"Singh","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Mem0.ai, research@mem0.ai"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Deshraj","family":"Yadav","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Mem0.ai, research@mem0.ai"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3233\/faia251160","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,21]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable prowess in generating contextually coherent responses, yet their fixed context windows pose fundamental challenges for maintaining consistency over prolonged multi-session dialogues. We introduce Mem0, a scalable memory-centric architecture that addresses this issue by dynamically extracting, consolidating, and retrieving salient information from ongoing conversations. Building on this foundation, we further propose an enhanced variant that leverages graph-based memory representations to capture complex relational structures among conversational elements. Through comprehensive evaluations on the LOCOMO benchmark, we systematically compare our approaches against six baseline categories. Empirical results demonstrate that our methods consistently outperform all existing memory systems across four question categories: single-hop, temporal, multi-hop, and open-domain. Notably, Mem0 achieves 26% relative improvements in the LLM-as-a-Judge metric over OpenAI, while Mem0 with graph memory achieves around 2% higher overall score than the base Mem0 configuration. Beyond accuracy gains, we also markedly reduce computational overhead compared to the full-context approach. In particular, Mem0 attains a 91% lower p95 latency and saves more than 90% token cost, thereby offering a compelling balance between advanced reasoning capabilities and practical deployment constraints. Our findings highlight the critical role of structured, persistent memory mechanisms for long-term conversational coherence, paving the way for more reliable and efficient LLM-driven AI agents. Code: https:\/\/mem0.ai\/research.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Frontiers in Artificial Intelligence and Applications","ECAI 2025"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.022","title":["Knowledge Graphs and Ontologies"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.022","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.artint.2023.103975","title":["Budget-feasible mechanisms for proportionally selecting agents from groups"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6672-5870","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xiang","family":"Liu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hau","family":"Chan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7370-6237","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Minming","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Weiwei","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8362-6735","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yingchao","family":"Zhao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.artint.2023.103975","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,10]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,10]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1088\/978-0-7503-6169-9ch9","title":["Memristive systems in image processing and artificial intelligence"],"author":[{"given":"Shaibal","family":"Mukherjee","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Technology Indore","place":["India"]},{"name":"QuanTechL2M Innovations Pvt. Ltd.","place":["India"]}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/978-0-7503-6169-9ch9","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]},"container-title":["Resistive Switching Systems for In-Memory Computation and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0014398600004052","title":["Empowering Financial Controlling with Artificial Intelligence: An Empirical Evaluation"],"author":[{"given":"Korbinian","family":"Markl","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Business Administration, Technical University of Applied Sciences Rosenheim, Hochschulstrasse 1, 83024 Rosenheim, Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Michael","family":"Diener","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Regensburg, Universit\u00e4tsstra\u00dfe 31, 93053 Regensburg, Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Michaela","family":"Polz","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Business Administration, Technical University of Applied Sciences Rosenheim, Hochschulstrasse 1, 83024 Rosenheim, Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Felix","family":"R\u00f6\u00dfle","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Business Administration, Technical University of Applied Sciences Rosenheim, Hochschulstrasse 1, 83024 Rosenheim, Germany"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0014398600004052","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 18th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.engappai.2024.109771","title":["Integrating Belief-Desire-Intention agents with large language models for reliable human\u2013robot interaction and explainable Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-5751-2831","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Laurent","family":"Frering","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Gerald","family":"Steinbauer-Wagner","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6786-5194","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Andreas","family":"Holzinger","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.engappai.2024.109771","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,2]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,2]]},"container-title":["Engineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011621","title":["Artificial Intelligence Controlled Manufacturing Strategies for New Energy Vehicles"],"author":[{"given":"Paul Sundar","family":"Singh","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Vels Institute of Science, Technology &#x0026; Advanced Studies (VISTAS),Department of Computer Science,Chennai,India"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Priya","family":"R","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Vels Institute of Science, Technology &#x0026; Advanced Studies (VISTAS),Department of Computer Applications,Chennai,India"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011621","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"container-title":["2025 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp;amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.020","title":["Representing Individuals and Relations"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.020","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.caeai.2026.100593","title":["Modelling individual participants as LLM agents in collaborative problem solving simulations"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9856-109X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zheng","family":"Fang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.caeai.2026.100593","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,6]]},"container-title":["Computers and Education: Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.5220\/0013145200003890","title":["Integration of Emotionally Intelligent Artificial Intelligence into Neuromarketing: Attitudes, Opportunities, Challenges"],"author":[{"given":"Ana","family":"Todorova","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Ruse \u201cAngel Kanchev\u201d, 8 Studentska Street, Ruse, Bulgaria"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Irina","family":"Kostadinova","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Ruse \u201cAngel Kanchev\u201d, 8 Studentska Street, Ruse, Bulgaria"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5220\/0013145200003890","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 17th International Conference on Agents and Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1201\/9781003410980-5","title":["Memory in Dendritic Spines"],"author":[{"given":"Huijue","family":"Jia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1201\/9781003410980-5","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,30]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,3,30]]},"container-title":["Neuroscience for Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011588","title":["Cognitive Large Language Model in Social Media with Local Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Vigneshwaran","family":"N","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"R.M.K. Engineering College,Department of IT,Chennai,601206"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"A.","family":"Vijayaraj","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"R.M.K. Engineering College,Department of IT,Chennai,601206"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"V. P.","family":"Murugan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Panimalar Engineering College,Department of Mathematics,Chennai,600 123"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R.","family":"Jebakumar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SRM Institute of Science and Technology,Department of Computing Technologies,Chennai"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"N.","family":"Mageshkumar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Madanapalle Institute of Technology &#x0026; Science,Department of Computer Science and Technology,Andhra Pradesh,517325"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R.","family":"Megavannan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"SRM Institute of Science and Technology,Faculty of Management"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011588","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"container-title":["2025 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp;amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>As artificial intelligence (AI) and its applications continue to reshape our world, understanding its historical roots becomes increasingly crucial. However, this historical perspective, focused on documenting what actually happened from the most objective point of view, is incomplete if we do not capture how different groups remember those events. For this reason, we argue in this paper in favor of developing a collective memory of AI in three different lines (as a body of knowledge, as attributes, and as a process) which will complement the historical task. As a result, we will obtain a more comprehensive vision of the development of AI, incorporating a more humanistic perspective, which will be crucial to understanding how society assesses AI.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1177\/30504554261417571","title":["A Proposal for a Collective Memory of Artificial Intelligence in Europe"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1982-2472","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Martin","family":"Pereira-Fari\u00f1a","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Instituto de Investigaci\u00f3n en Humanidades (iHUS), Universidade Santiago de Compostela, Santiago de Compostela, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2025-6559","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Davide","family":"Bassi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Centro Singular de Investigaci\u00f3n en Tecnolox\u00edas Intelixentes (CiTIUS), Universidade de Santiago de Compostela, Santiago de Compostela, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,12]]},"container-title":["The European Journal on Artificial Intelligence"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,12]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1177\/30504554261417571"},{"DOI":"10.1201\/9781003374404-14","title":["Quantum Associative Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Andreas","family":"Wichert","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1201\/9781003374404-14","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,28]]},"container-title":["Quantum Artificial Intelligence with Qiskit"]},{"DOI":"10.1609\/aaai.v40i30.39773","title":["ARTEM: Enhancing Large Language Model Agents with Spatial-Temporal Episodic Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Cassandra Hui-Ming","family":"Tan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Budhitama","family":"Subagdja","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ah-Hwee","family":"Tan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1609\/aaai.v40i30.39773","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,14]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Current large language models (LLMs) exhibit significant deficiencies in episodic memory tasks including encoding, storing, and retrieving specific information from temporally dependent events over a long period of time. Recent approaches to handle memory tasks in LLMs, such as in-context learning, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and fine-tuning, may resolve the long-term retention issues, but are still inadequate to handle tasks requiring chronological awareness of the stored information. We introduce Agentic Retrieval with Temporal-Episodic Memory (ARTEM), a hybrid LLM-based agent architecture integrating LLMs with a self-organizing neural network named Spatial-Temporal Episodic Memory (STEM), designed to handle episodic memory tasks. Our approach employs LLMs for event extraction from the inputs to represent temporal, spatial, entitative, and semantic information that may facilitate future retrieval, aside from generating outputs or direct responses. The extracted events can then be encoded vectorially and stored in a fast and stable manner in the episodic memory through an instance-based incremental learning in STEM. STEM supports precise episodes retrieval and helps reduce computational overhead in generating the appropriate responses by LLMs. Evaluation on standardized episodic memory benchmarks across four tasks\u2014partial cue retrieval, epistemic uncertainty detection, recent event identification, and chronological recall\u2014demonstrates superior performance of ARTEM compared to in-context learning, RAG, and fine-tuning in various popular LLMs.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.artint.2023.104050","title":["Negotiation strategies for agents with ordinal preferences: Theoretical analysis and human study"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9910-0762","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Noam","family":"Hazon","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sefi","family":"Erlich","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3230-3060","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ariel","family":"Rosenfeld","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Sarit","family":"Kraus","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.artint.2023.104050","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,2]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,2]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011857","title":["Artificial Intelligence in Phishing Detection and Analysis: A Foundational Review"],"author":[{"given":"C.","family":"Rajeswari","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Chennai Institute of Technology,Dept. of CSE (Cybersecurity),Chennai,India"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Rajeeth Prabhu.","family":"S","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Chennai Institute of Technology,Dept. of CSE (Cybersecurity),Chennai,India"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai65575.2025.11011857","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,28]]},"container-title":["2025 International Conference on Data Science, Agents &amp;amp; Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/icdsaai69492.2026.11505142","title":["Artificial Intelligence Enabled Human Gait Recognition System for Viewpoint Aware Visual Surveillance"],"author":[{"given":"K.","family":"Sabitha","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Chennai Institute of Technology, Kundrathur,Department of Computer Science and Engineering,Chennai,Tamil Nadu,India,600069"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R.","family":"Janarthanan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Chennai Institute of Technology, Kundrathur,Department of Computer Science and Engineering,Chennai,Tamil Nadu,India,600069"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icdsaai69492.2026.11505142","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"container-title":["2026 International Conference on Data Science, Agents and Artificial Intelligence (ICDSAAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.005","title":["Reasoning and Planning with Certainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.005","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]},{"DOI":"10.1017\/9781009258227.010","title":["Learning and Reasoning with Uncertainty"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1017\/9781009258227.010","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,13]]},"container-title":["Artificial Intelligence"]}],"items-per-page":100,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}